\label{rem-quadmin}
    The same proof shows an essentially equivalent statement: for any $\lambda>0$, the functional
    \begin{equation*}
       x\mapsto\;\; -\min_{y\in K}\langle x, y\rangle+\frac{1}{2\lambda}\|x\|^2,
    \end{equation*}
    obtains the minimum at the point $\lambda x^*\in \lambda K$.

Using a random search program in \cite{yao_program_2025}, we have
found many unstable non-Delzant polygons, Figure \ref{fig:A-relatively-K-unstable} is an example.  
\begin{figure}[h]
\begin{centering}
\includegraphics[viewport=130bp 155bp 720bp 435bp,clip,scale=0.4]{example_Kunstable}
\par\end{centering}
\caption{\label{fig:A-relatively-K-unstable}A relatively K-unstable pentagon. }
